  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Adjetivos para describir lugares y personas (con su opuesto)**",
      "",
      "| Adjetivo | Opuesto |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| quiet (tranquilo) | noisy (ruidoso) |",
      "| clean (limpio) | dirty (sucio) |",
      "| safe (seguro) | dangerous (peligroso) |",
      "| cheap (barato) | expensive (caro) |",
      "| big (grande) | small (pequeño) |",
      "| old (viejo, antiguo) | new (nuevo) / modern (moderno) |",
      "",
      "**Más adjetivos:** *beautiful, ugly, friendly, boring, exciting, crowded, popular, lovely*.",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** los adjetivos no cambian por género ni número: *a quiet town, quiet towns*. Van **antes** del sustantivo o después de *to be*: *It's a clean city. The city is clean.*",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *dangerous* /ˈdeɪndʒərəs/ · *expensive* /ɪkˈspensɪv/ (acento en -pen-) · *crowded* /ˈkraʊdɪd/.",
      "",
      "**Modificar los adjetivos (¿cuánto?)**",
      "",
      "| Palabra | Significado | Ejemplo |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **very / really / extremely** | muy, muchísimo | *The city is **very** noisy. · It's **really** exciting.* |",
      "| **quite / fairly** | bastante | *It's **quite** expensive.* |",
      "| **a bit / a little** | un poco | *The hotel is **a bit** small.* |",
      "| **not very / not at all** | no muy / nada | *It isn't **very** big. · It isn't **at all** dangerous.* |",
      "| **too** | demasiado (problema) | *It's **too** crowded for me.* |",
      "",
      "Van **antes** del adjetivo. **Ojo:** *much* no modifica adjetivos (*much big* ✗ → *very big* ✓) y *very* no se usa con adjetivos ya extremos (*very amazing* ✗ → *really amazing* ✓)."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "It's a noise city.",
        "right": "It's a noisy city.",
        "note": "Para describir se necesita el adjetivo noisy."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "The streets are cleans.",
        "right": "The streets are clean.",
        "note": "El adjetivo no lleva -s en plural."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": [
      {
        "word": "sensible",
        "es_false": "sensible",
        "real": "sensato/a",
        "note": "Sensible = sensato. Sensible (emocional) se dice sensitive."
      }
    ]
  },
